When a `file://` URL contains query parameters (e.g., `file:///Users/secret/doc.pdf?token=xyz`), the current logic hits the `url.query != nil` branch first and returns `file:///Users/secret/doc.pdf?[REDACTED_QUERY]`, leaking the full filesystem path. Consider checking for `file://` scheme before redacting the query.

